# The gripper as tool 2 on the changer (arcmate_changer.arm: its drive,
# jaws 190 mm out = its TCP; `gripper tool 2`): picked from its dock, a
# 2 kg part gripped at the TCP (flange forward and up, B 45: the
# part turned with it), weighed on the lift on top of the tool's own 1.8 kg (both
# in the detector's model: tool from the changer's monitor, part from the
# grip), put down, released; the gripper back in its dock: its jaws do
# nothing there (closing empty). No collision hit, no fault.
@program arm/arm_sim
@args arm/arcmate/arcmate_changer.arm
part box1 1.15 0 1.10   0.015 0.02 0.02   2.0   0 45 0
detector arm/arcmate/model_perturbed.arm
lcnc 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1
run 1.5
mark
@include arm/tests/inc_tool_pick2.txt
lmove 2 1150 -100 1100 0 45 0
run 2.2
lmove 1 1150 0 1100 0 45 0
run 1.2
grip expect 30 2.0 0 0 0.19
grip close
run 1.5
tlmove 1.0 1150 0 1250 0 45 0
run 1.2
print grip
tlmove 1.0 1150 0 1100 0 45 0
run 1.2
grip open
run 1.5
lmove 1 1150 -100 1100 0 45 0
run 1.2
print grip
@include arm/tests/inc_tool_drop2.txt
grip expect 0 0 0 0 0.19
grip close
run 2.5
print grip tool coll off
@expect arm.grip_state[1] == 2
@expect arm.grip_width[1] > 29.5
@expect arm.grip_width[1] < 30.2
@expect arm.pay_state[1] == 3
@expect arm.pay_meas[1] > 1.0
@expect arm.pay_meas[1] < 3.0
@expect arm.part_z[1] > 1240
@expect arm.grip_state[2] == 0
@expect arm.pay_model[2] == 0
@expect arm.grip_held[2] == -1
@expect arm.tool_mounted[-1] == 0
@expect arm.grip_held[-1] == -1
@expect arm.grip_state[-1] == 4
@expect arm.coll == 0
@expect arm.off_reason == 0
@reject ^ERROR
